// @run
// @log 1
// @warning Unused function `mk`
// The SILENT cell of the alias-blind nullable closure at the RETURN position: the function
// is declared and never called, so nothing downstream can reject it and the only observable
// is the module's own validity.
//
// On the parent this program built a module wasmtime refuses to compile
// (`failed to compile: wasm[0]::function[5]::mk`) while its INLINE twin
// (`function mk(): ((i32) => i32) | null { inc }`) printed 1. `wasmEmit`'s `retNulClosure`
// asks `nulCloFlag(fn.fnRet)`, whose arena leg wants `TyNullable(TyFunc)` and was handed
// `TyNullable(TyUnion[TyFunc])` by the one-member `UnionDecl` the parser builds for an
// arrow-bodied alias, while `emit_sections`' `vtKindOfType` wrote the closure result
// valtype — the two halves of the return disagreed. D-ALIASFN makes the alias denote its
// member, so both read the same thing.
//
// `mk` is deliberately left UNUSED (hence the declared warning) rather than `_`-prefixed:
// CALLING it and reading the result is a clean emit reject on BOTH sides and for the INLINE
// spelling too (`emitProgram: bare null needs a struct-typed context`) — that gap is not
// alias-specific and is not what this pins.

type F = (i32) => i32

function inc(a: i32) { a + 1 }

function mk(): F | null { inc }

print(1)
